[89.461204, "o", "s = p.read_text().replace('- Sender not delegated:', '- An explicit DMARC failure in the mail drop\\'s `Authentication-Results`\\n  holds the message for manual sender verification, even if From is delegated.\\n  These headers must be supplied by a trusted inbound mail drop.\\n- Sender not delegated:')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.461288, "o", "start = s.index('## Known gaps (0.4)')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.461353, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.461386, "o", "end = s.index('## Handoffs', start)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[89.461404, "o", "> "]
[89.461467, "o", "s = s[:start] + '''## Handler completion\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[89.461517, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.461602, "o", "Revocations, transitive implied roles (including cycles), idempotent grants,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.461626, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[89.46171, "o", "> comma-separated role lists, normalized sender matching, held/rejected auditing,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.461725, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[89.461736, "o", "> "]
[89.461831, "o", "and write-free dry runs are implemented and covered by tests. Dry runs simulate\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.461922, "o", "requests in queue order, including minimum-holder checks, without persisting\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.461944, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.462023, "o", "any changes. Malformed messages retain available ticket/sender metadata in the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[89.462133, "o", "audit log; unavailable metadata uses `?` for ticket and empty strings otherwise.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[89.46215, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.462156, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[89.462257, "o", "> ''' + s[end:]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p.write_text(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
